# Accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AA)

## Must

- Text contrast ≥ **4.5:1** (large text ≥ 3:1). Non-text UI (icons, focus) ≥ **3:1**.
- Visible **`:focus-visible`** outline ≥ 2px with ≥ 3:1 contrast vs unfocused state. Never `outline: none` without a replacement.
- Pointer targets ≥ **24×24 CSS px** (or sufficient spacing). Prefer ≥ 44px on primary mobile actions.
- Buttons and links have real accessible names (not icon-only without `aria-label`).
- Forms: visible labels (`<label for>` or wrapping). Errors are text, not color-only.
- Keyboard: full Tab path; no keyboard traps. Drag/reorder has a non-drag alternative.
- Map: always ship a **list view** of the same places (BRD §10.4).
- Images: meaningful `alt`; decorative images `alt=""`.

## Motion

```css
/* tokens.css already disables animation under reduced motion — keep it */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *, *::before, *::after {
    animation: none !important;
    transition: none !important;
  }
}
```

Do not add river-ripple or scroll animations that ignore `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Language

- Set `document.documentElement.lang` to `hi` or `en` when the language toggle changes.
- Devanagari names sit beside English where place names appear.
